<title>MEXICO: Bital merges units to boost capital.</title>
<headline>Bital merges units to boost capital.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grupo Financiero Bital said on Tuesday its shareholders approved the incorporation of 10 subsidiaries into the capital of its bank, Banco Internacional.</p>
<p>In a statement, it said the subsidiaries included its foreign exchange house, Casa de Cambio Bital, its factoring unit, Factor Bital, and its leasing arm, Arrendadora Bital.</p>
<p>The banking group also said Banco Internacional shareholders agreed to acquire between September 24 and October 8, 15,517,619 new A and B shares, at the rate of 9.85355879271 per 100 ACP or BCP issues, at a price of 8 pesos per share.</p>
<p>--Claudia Villegas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9549</p>
